This work presents SMAUG-SCA: the first power side-channel analysis (SCA) attack on SMAUG-T, the Korean post-quantum crypto (KpqC) Key Encapsulation Mechanism (KEM) standard. Although KpqC standardization was concluded in 2025, the side-channel analysis (SCA) of SMAUG-T has not been investigated in detail until now. SMAUG-SCA utilizes Random Forest, XGBoost, and a Fully Connected Neural Network (FCN) to achieve a test accuracy of > 94%, showing that the secret key can be recovered with < 10 traces with a success probability of > 99.9%.